    {
        "content": "<p>yes, you can use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Quotient#doc\">docs#Quotient</a></p>",
        "id": 579719375,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773671005
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>the quotient map is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Quotient.mk#doc\">docs#Quotient.mk</a>, that it is constant on equivalence classes is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Quotient.sound#doc\">docs#Quotient.sound</a>, and making functions which factor through the quotient is given by <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Quotient.lift#doc\">docs#Quotient.lift</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Quotient.lift_mk#doc\">docs#Quotient.lift_mk</a></p>",
